      "status": "completed",
      "text": "Esther: \"You're staring.\"\nSimon: \"Yeah. You don't wear these at home.\"\nEsther: \"You don't wear clothes at home.\"\nSimon: \"That's my point.\"\nEsther: \"Are we still strangers?\"\nSimon: \"We don't need to be. It's been long enough.\"\nEsther: \"Is it?\"\n\nSimon sits up in bed, the sheet around his waist. His hands flutter restlessly, searching for a place to land. The room is bare.\nEsther: \"If I was anyone else, would I be allowed to see you naked?\"\nSimon: \"Why would you be anyone else?\"\nEsther: \"I'm a stranger to myself.\"\n\nEsther closes her eyes. \"That's not a compliment,\" she says, and moves off the bed toward the window.",
